       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for an adult.\n\n- **Daily maximum:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for inpatients. Over-the-counter use is limited to 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single-dose maximum:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose. Doses above that add no benefit and raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nNormal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't change this.\n\nHere are some common regimens I could enter instead:\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day) for mild to moderate pain\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), for inflammatory conditions\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n\nWas 1600 mg meant to be the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily? Or did you intend a different dose? Tell me which regimen you want, and I'll enter it. If you do want the original dose, please confirm the clinical rationale."
